{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1427821-chimersty-and-auras","id":1427821,"title":"Chimersty and Auras","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-12-09T00:15:18-08:00","id":1427821,"title":"Chimersty and Auras","content":"Can chimerstry be used to mask auras? Even if only for a short period of time. Like when they know someone might be reading their aura.<br /> <br /> A ravnos in the chronicle I run just Diablerized someone and they are going to want to hide it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-09T00:52:49-08:00","id":1427825,"title":"","content":"Through combo discipline or an elder power, probably. Through normal 1-5 powers, no. You can only make 'physical' constructs with 1-5 chimestry. <br /> <br /> Chimestry can't take away from stuff, it can only add. You could only mask that aura by adding stuff to it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-09T05:31:23-08:00","id":1427846,"title":"","content":"As far as I know, the only way to to imbue emotion into an illusion is with Chimerstry 6: False Resonance from V20. Which is not to say a player couldn't develop a combo-discipline to do it. Just perhaps not on the timescale necessary to hide suddenly acquired diablerie stains...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/699-malleusxxiii","name":"MalleusXXIII","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar699_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-09T11:35:09-08:00","id":1427883,"title":"","content":"With Chimerstry, maybe not. However, I seem to remember reading somewhere of an Obfuscate power (possibly a combo with Auspex) that can change an aura. A similar power should be available with Chimerstry, especially a combo with Obfuscate. Such a power could also hide one's vampiric nature as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>THWarted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/17984-toby-weingarten","name":"Toby Weingarten","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-09T12:44:35-08:00","id":1427894,"title":"","content":"Thank you all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-09T16:39:07-08:00","id":1427921,"titl